                    "total_reviews": 14556
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237512721",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198330018091",
                            "num_reviews": 27,
                            "playtime_forever": 724,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 724,
                            "last_played": 1682692171
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is one of the few times I go and do a longer review for a game that means so much to me.\n\nBefore playing this game, I was probably in the worst state of my life I had ever been; nothing was working out for me during that time with relationships, work/school, debt and mental health at all times low.\n\nThen one night I just decided to play this game since the praise was so high and I just needed to take my mind off for a few hours; I didn't think I would resonate with a character to such a deep level like that. The way Jill thought and saw stuff was on such a level that I got scared about how connected I felt to a fictional character. She is literally me, I kept thinking. The vibe and the setting of the game were such an immense feeling; I was just cuddled up in my chair in the dark playing this very bright and colourful game, with the amazing soundtrack of Garoad. And just taking in all the characters' stories unfolds as you just sit there and listen.\n\nAs the game progressed, I kept crying more and more about how the story unfolds. It felt like the game was talking to me personally and directly, as if it knew exactly what my life situation looked like. Just like how this game was MADE for me, I finally felt like something in my brain told me for the first time ever exactly what I was doing wrong, and I needed to change if I wanted to be happy and change my ways moving forward.\n\nFor that alone I will forever love this game and Jill Stingray. Literally changed my life for the better, and I will forever cherish what it did to me. I see life differently today, and I'm proud of how far I come since I beat this game in 2023.\n\nI love life, and I love VA-11 Hall-A",
